# mm.sdcard.socket

The board's TF socket, as a block device a portable program mounts without
naming a pin: mm::fs::fat::mount("/sd", mm::sdcard::socket::card()). A board
whose socket is wired to an SPI bus binds a provider that owns an
mm.sdcard SpiCard on the socket's pins, as a display board binds its panel;
the card initialises on first use, so an empty socket costs nothing until it
is read.

A program reaching mm.sdcard.socket is unavailable on a board that binds no
provider. With none bound, the fallback's card answers Unsupported to
everything.
